WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.650
moisture sensor. App demo with a simulated device. The real desktop app, driven by a simulated device that speaks the firmware protocol. Synthetic readings.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.200
A probe in the rice changes an oscillator frequency

3
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:05.300
The ESP32 turns frequency into moisture, plus temperature and humidity

4
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.800
Readings stream over USB serial as moisture, temperature, humidity

5
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:08.850
The desktop app stores them for analysis and export

6
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.650
The app finds the device on USB serial (a simulated device here)

7
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:12.950
Start Collection: the device runs its measurement loops

8
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.950
Five loops of 37.5 seconds each, sped up here

9
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.100
Collection complete, every reading saved to SQLite

10
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.550
Show Graph opens the analysis window

11
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.450
Average, median and mode, with a status: optimal at 12 to 14 percent

12
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.950
The chart plots the last five readings, synthetic here

13
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.650
moisture sensor. Real host app on a simulated device. No hardware footage; readings are synthetic.

